# Tomcat RewriteValve rules for the tablet server, Host level (conf/Catalina/localhost/rewrite.config).
#
# 🔴 TOMCAT MATCHES THE WHOLE PATH, NOT A PREFIX. RewriteRule and RewriteCond both call
# Matcher.matches(), so `^/rest/videos` refuses `/rest/videos` and nothing under it. Every pattern here
# therefore spells out what may follow (`(/.*)?$`). The first version of the two upload rules was
# written as prefixes and let `/rest/videos/` through (fixed 2026-10-22, before it ever deployed).
#
# ── 1. The two public uploads, refused on EVERY hostname ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Owner, 2026-10-22: "close the tablet server's open upload path". Two Headwind endpoints accept a
# file upload with no sign-in, and nothing on this fleet uses either:
#   /rest/public/applications/upload   the desktop "AppList" utility's door
#   /rest/videos                       a video upload outside /rest/private, so no JWT filter runs on it
RewriteRule ^/rest/public/applications/upload(/.*)?$ - [F,NC]
RewriteRule ^/rest/videos(/.*)?$ - [F,NC]
#
# ── 2. The host split: every name except the console serves the tablets' paths and nothing else ───
# Owner, 2026-10-22: "split the Headwind console onto mdm-console behind Access". One Tomcat serves the
# console, the private API and the tablet API on every name pointed at it, so mdm.satopharma.com —
# which can never carry Access, or the fleet goes dark — exposed the console and the token endpoint
# (/rest/public/jwt/login, which skips two-factor). From here the console, the private API and the
# token endpoint answer ONLY on mdm-console.satopharma.com, which sits behind Cloudflare Access and
# whose requests the add-on's AccessGateFilter checks for a valid Access pass.
#
# The allowlist is every call the tablet agent makes, read from its own source
# (app/src/main/java/com/hmdm/launcher/server/ServerService.java, plus PushNotificationWorker,
# PushLongPollingService and GetServerConfigTask) at h-mdm/hmdm-android master AND at our launcher
# fork's tag launcher-6.39-r1, which changes no endpoint — plus /files/, where every APK the
# configuration hands a tablet lives. Add a path here only from the agent's source, never from a guess:
# a path missing from this list is a tablet that stops syncing, with the server looking healthy.
#
# The host test is %{HTTP_HOST}, which Tomcat resolves to request.getServerName() (the Host header
# without its port). AccessGateFilter tests the same value, so the two can never disagree about which
# requests are the console's.
RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} !^mdm-console\.satopharma\.com$ [NC]
RewriteRule !^/(files/.+|rest/public/sync/configuration/[^/]+|rest/public/sync/info|rest/notifications/device/[^/]+|rest/notification/polling/[^/]+|rest/plugins/devicelog/log/(rules|list)/[^/]+|rest/plugins/deviceinfo/deviceinfo/public/[^/]+|rest/plugins/deviceinfo/deviceinfo-plugin-settings/device/[^/]+|rest/plugins/devicelocations/public/update/[^/]+|rest/plugins/devicereset/public/((reboot|password)/)?[^/]+)$ - [F]
#
# Only RewriteRule and RewriteCond lines and comments belong here: RewriteCheck.java parses this file
# with Tomcat's own parser at image build, then runs Tomcat's own engine over a list of real tablet,
# console and refused requests, and fails the build on any surprise — because a line Tomcat cannot
# parse fails the whole Host at start while Railway still reports the deploy green, and a rule that
# parses but refuses a tablet path takes the fleet dark just as quietly.
